WEBVTT

asr-000001
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:17.540
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: For the record, House Bill No. 10858 has been formally referred to the Committee on Appropriations.

asr-000002
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.360
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: According to today's proceedings, it shall be conducted as a budget hearing on the bill.

asr-000003
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:28.500
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: I would like to acknowledge the members and our resource persons.

asr-000004
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.860
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: From the Commission on Human Rights,

asr-000005
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.740
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: The Attorney Richard P. Palato, our Chairperson,

asr-000006
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.760
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Attorney Beda Epres,

asr-000007
00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:45.240
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Attorney Feda Dumarpa,

asr-000008
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.080
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Commissioner Justin Monina Sinarosa,

asr-000009
00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.800
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Commissioner Judge Maria Amifate Fider Reyes,

asr-000010
00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.560
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Executive Director-Attorney Jacqueline Andiguilla,

asr-000011
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.800
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: and also our Acting Executive Director, Lawrence Charles Isalazar,

asr-000012
00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:12.180
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: from Human Rights Violation Victims Memorial Commission.

asr-000013
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.800
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Good afternoon po sa mga taga...

asr-000014
00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:15.620
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Commission on Human Rights.

asr-000015
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:23.520
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: And of course, gusto ko rin pong i-acknowledge ang aking mga kasamahan sa mababang kongreso,

asr-000016
00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:27.720
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: ang tatlo sa masisipag kong kasamahan sa kongreso.

asr-000017
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.940
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Siyempre po ang ating Deputy Minority Leader,

asr-000018
00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.560
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Congressman Percy Sandano from Akbayan Partylist,

asr-000019
00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:40.200
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Representative Dada Kiram Ismula from Akbayan Partylist,

asr-000020
00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.240
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: and also Assistant Minority Leader, Rene Co. of Kabatayan,

asr-000021
00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:45.260
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: and Party List.

asr-000022
00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.460
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: And siyempre po, presentin po ang ating pong Civil Society Organization,

asr-000023
00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:56.360
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Attorney Obe de la Cruz, National Coalition for the Family and Constitution,

asr-000024
00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.660
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Distinguished members of the Committee on Appropriations,

asr-000025
00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.980
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: my esteemed colleagues in the House of Representatives,

asr-000026
00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.980
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Officials and Personnel of the Commission on Human Rights,

asr-000027
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.520
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: magandang hapon po sa ating lahat.

asr-000028
00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.140
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Allow me to begin by...

asr-000029
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.860
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: putting the CHR budget in perspective through one figure

asr-000030
00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:31.700
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: that I hope will remain with this committee throughout this day,

asr-000031
00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:36.300
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: deliberation of 0.02%.

asr-000032
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:43.780
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Sa kabuang 7.2 trillion proposed national budget for 2027,

asr-000033
00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:50.460
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: the Commission on Human Rights is provided 1.273 billion pesos

asr-000034
00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.200
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: under National Expenditure Program,

asr-000035
00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.340
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: or just 0.02% of the entire national budget.

asr-000036
00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:04.640
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: The CHR, however, proposed a total budget of 2.749 billion pesos.

asr-000037
00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.340
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Even if Congress were to provide this entire amount,

asr-000038
00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:13.880
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: it will still account for only around 0.04% of the national budget,

asr-000039
00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.840
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: from 0.02% provided under the NEP,

asr-000040
00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:23.100
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: to 0.04% if the entire CHR proposal were funded.

asr-000041
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.180
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Ganoon po kaliit ang hinihing bahagi ng Commission on Human Rights

asr-000042
00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.120
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: mula sa ating pambansang pundo.

asr-000043
00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:36.120
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Yet the responsibility entrusted to this constitutional institution

asr-000044
00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.560
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: is anything but small.

asr-000045
00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:44.940
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: The CHR remains among the lowest funded institution of the national government,

asr-000046
00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.700
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: yet its mandate extends across the country

asr-000047
00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.180
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: and touches the lives and rights of every Filipino.

asr-000048
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.440
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: We expect the Commission to investigate,

asr-000049
00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:59.520
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: allege human rights violations and assist victims.

asr-000050
00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:05.260
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: We expect it to monitor jails and other places of deprivation of liberty,

asr-000051
00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.140
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: help prevent torture and abuse,

asr-000052
00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.720
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: educate our people about their rights,

asr-000053
00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.840
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: and advise Congress and government on human rights laws and policies.

asr-000054
00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:23.180
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Habang lumalaki po at nagiging komplikado ang haman sa karapatang pantao,

asr-000055
00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:28.440
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: kailangan din po natin tiyakin na meron po tayong sapat na kakayanan

asr-000056
00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:34.780
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: at resources ang institusyong inaatasan ng ating konstitusyon para tumugon sa mga ito.

asr-000057
00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:41.040
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Mga kasama, we cannot continue to demand more from our constitutional institution

asr-000058
00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.480
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: without ensuring that it has the resources necessary

asr-000059
00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:50.760
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: to effectively perform the responsibilities to entrust it.

asr-000060
00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.160
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: And let us also be careful.

asr-000061
00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:53.560
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: We need to be clear.

asr-000062
00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.700
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: The CHR is not advisory of government.

asr-000063
00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:01.980
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Kakampi po natin ang CHR sa mabuting pamamahala.

asr-000064
00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:09.120
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Ang independent and adequately funded CHR helps government identify gaps,

asr-000065
00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:14.280
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: prevent abuses, protect vulnerable sectors, and strengthen accountability.

asr-000066
00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.840
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: When the CHR tells us where government can do better,

asr-000067
00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:22.840
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: it helps us build stronger and more accountable,

asr-000068
00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.200
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: more responsible institutions.

asr-000069
00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:32.700
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: This is why the budget before us should not be viewed simply as funding for another government office.

asr-000070
00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:41.700
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: When we invest in CHR, we invest in justice, accountability, good governance, and human dignity.

asr-000071
00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:45.700
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Kaya habang sinisimulan po natin ang debilirasyon ito,

asr-000072
00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:51.700
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: I ask my distinguished colleagues, tatatlo po tayong nandito ngayon,

asr-000073
00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:57.039
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Consider not only how much? Apat na po ba?

asr-000073-split-2
00:05:57.039 --> 00:05:59.800
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Apat na.

asr-000074
00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:04.000
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: consider not only how much we can afford to provide the CHR,

asr-000075
00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:09.680
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: but also what we expect the Commission to accomplish with the resources we give.

asr-000076
00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:16.040
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: After all, while CHR is provided only 0.02% of our national budget,

asr-000077
00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:22.040
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: the right it is constitutionally mandated to protect belongs to

asr-000078
00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.500
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: one hundred percent of the Filipino people.

asr-000079
00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:29.760
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: With that, may I request the Chairperson of the Commission on Human Rights,

asr-000080
00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:34.300
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Chairperson Richard Palpal frase

asr-000081
00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.300
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: to begin with their presentation.

asr-000082
00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.300
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000083
00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.300
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Thank you Your Honour.

asr-000084
00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.300
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The Honorable Chairperson,

asr-000085
00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:47.300
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Distinguished Members of the Committee on Appropriations,

asr-000086
00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.300
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: fellow public servants and everyone present today.

asr-000087
00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.300
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Magandang hapon po sa ating lahat.

asr-000088
00:06:51.300 --> 00:07:04.200
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: I am pleased to present the Commission on Human Rights proposed budget for fiscal year 2027 along with our accomplishment for 2025 and the first semester of 2026 and targets for 2027.

asr-000089
00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:16.720
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: For most, I would like to thank our budget sponsor, Representative Maria Cristina Talavera Lopez, for her opening statement and continued advocacy and support for the CHR.

asr-000090
00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:27.400
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The CHR's proposed budget aims to strengthen the Commission's delivery of services in line with its constitutional mandate for human rights protection and promotion,

asr-000091
00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:38.600
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: prevention of human rights violations in places of deprivation of liberty, and policy advisory services to strengthen the Philippine government's compliance with its human rights obligations.

asr-000092
00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:46.600
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: In terms of operations, the CHR has 726

asr-000093
00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:58.400
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: out of 836 plantilla positions across the central office and 17 regional offices as of August 2026. With the permission of the Chair,

asr-000094
00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:02.920
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Let me begin by sharing the CHR's budget allocation and utilization rate.

asr-000095
00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:10.080
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Historically, the CHR's annual obligation rate has averaged 95% since 2019.

asr-000096
00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:15.400
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The CHR strives to maintain its disbursement rate, which has stood at 100%.

asr-000097
00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:27.480
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Since 2024, and by the end of fiscal year 2026, it is estimated that the CHR will be able to maintain similar budget, obligation, and disbursement rates.

asr-000098
00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:39.780
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Now, allow me to present a detailed breakdown of the CHR's proposed budget for the fiscal year of 2027 in comparison with the 2027 National Expenditure Program.

asr-000099
00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:46.480
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: As shown in column 3, the CHR's original proposed budget for 2027 is 2.749 billion pesos.

asr-000100
00:08:46.720 --> 00:09:03.020
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: A total of 1.173 billion was proposed under Tier 1, while 1.576 billion was proposed under Tier 2.

asr-000101
00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:11.560
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The CHR's total allocation under the 2027 NEP has been reduced by almost 53%,

asr-000102
00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:17.880
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: which is equivalent to 1,272,592,000 pesos.

asr-000103
00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:36.540
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: As shown in column No. 5, there is a deficit of 1.477 billion in the 2027 NEP proposal compared to the CHR's proposal under Tiers 1 and 2.

asr-000104
00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:43.180
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: And this deficit mostly accounts for the Commission's capital outlay for 2027.

asr-000105
00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:48.080
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: As such, the breakdown of the CHR's 2027 NEP

asr-000106
00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:48.880
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: is as follows.

asr-000107
00:09:49.940 --> 00:10:02.920
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: 718,805,000 for personal services plus an additional 61.33 million for RLIP,

asr-000108
00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:08.540
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: or a total of 780,138,000.

asr-000109
00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:16.100
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: And for the maintenance and other operating expenses, 492,454,000.

asr-000110
00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:22.160
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Of course, the CHR is grateful to the Department of Budget and Management

asr-000111
00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:27.060
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: for recognizing two of the Commission's important Tier 2 requirements.

asr-000112
00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:31.960
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: As seen in the lower right-hand corner of the presentation,

asr-000113
00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:40.120
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Andiyan po, binigyan po tayo ng DBM ng 16,019,000

asr-000114
00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:48.040
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: for the visitorial mandate of the CHR through the expanded Places of Deprivation of Liberty,

asr-000115
00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:49.200
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: visitation program,

asr-000116
00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:58.820
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: at 19,300,000 out of the 59 million for the augmentation of mandatory expenses

asr-000117
00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:01.020
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: for central and regional offices.

asr-000118
00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:07.080
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: To provide further context, the next slide shows,

asr-000119
00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:15.840
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: compared with the 2026 GAA budget of 1.347 billion,

asr-000120
00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.840
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: the 2027 NEP,

asr-000121
00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:25.100
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: that only amounts to 1,272,592,000.

asr-000122
00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:31.100
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: May I invite you to please look at the figures listed in the last column.

asr-000123
00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:35.660
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: As seen in the row marked as grand total,

asr-000124
00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:43.540
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: there's an overall decrease of 74,882,000 out of the budget of the CHR.

asr-000125
00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:47.800
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The decrease is primarily due to the lack of capital outlay allocation

asr-000126
00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:49.800
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: in the 2027 NEP.

asr-000127
00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:56.800
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: For MOOE, there is a decrease amounting to a negative variance of 34,888,000.

asr-000128
00:11:56.800 --> 00:12:05.360
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: And for personal services, there's an increase amounting to 103,549,000

asr-000129
00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:10.800
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: due to the increase in the filled-up positions of the CHR

asr-000130
00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:16.960
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and the implementation of the fourth tranche of the updated salary standardization law,

asr-000131
00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:17.780
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and

asr-000132
00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:19.800
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: automatic appropriations for retirement or RLIP.

asr-000133
00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:29.080
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Now allow me now to illustrate how resources translate into actual services.

asr-000134
00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:36.080
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The CHR's constitutional mandate is discharged through the delivery of its programs in human rights protection,

asr-000135
00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:41.840
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: prevention of human rights violation, human rights promotion and policy advisory services.

asr-000136
00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:48.840
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So, for protection services, the CHR focuses on the documentation and management of complaints,

asr-000137
00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:49.840
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: human rights violations, and general policies.

asr-000138
00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:50.800
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So, for protection services, the CHR focuses on the documentation and management of complaints, human rights violations, and general policies.

asr-000139
00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:59.440
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: independent forensic services, legal assistance and counseling, financial assistance and witness protection, or security.

asr-000140
00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:15.320
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: In the first six months of 2026, the Commission received 2,942 cases of which 2,623 were already disposed or acted upon as of June 2026.

asr-000141
00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:31.680
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Ang breakdown po nito ay complaints received, meaning request for assistance, case investigation, and other protective services.

asr-000142
00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:44.680
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So through the Task Force Zero Backlog, the CHR has disposed of or acted upon 27,307 out of the 28,519

asr-000143
00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:53.540
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Backlog cases, leaving a total of 1,212 pending cases from 1987 to 2025.

asr-000144
00:13:54.820 --> 00:14:00.860
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: This represents substantial progress in addressing long-standing cases of human rights violations.

asr-000145
00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:09.020
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Now for the prevention services of the Commission.

asr-000146
00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:16.360
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So the CHR is mandated to conduct regular visitation and conduct preventive monitoring of human rights violations.

asr-000147
00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:18.760
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: conditions

asr-000148
00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:29.120
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: In places of deprivation of liberty such as jails, military and police custodial facilities, prison facilities, child-carest facilities and mental health facilities, among others.

asr-000149
00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:44.140
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: For visits in places of detention, the Commission conducted 960 POD visits in 2024 and in 2025, 985.

asr-000150
00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:45.380
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and the

asr-000158
00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:46.680
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: for the first semester.

asr-000159
00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:47.920
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: 2026,

asr-000160
00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.220
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: the CHR has visited

asr-000161
00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:53.280
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: 617 facilities.

asr-000162
00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:56.420
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Under the Commission's

asr-000163
00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:58.340
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Fostering Torture-Free

asr-000164
00:14:58.340 --> 00:14:59.980
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Facilities Initiative,

asr-000165
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:05.240
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The Commission focuses on detention facilities with highest incidences of torture

asr-000166
00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:13.740
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Under this program, the CHR conducted 136 visits across 24 facilities in 2025

asr-000167
00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:19.660
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and 16 visits across 12 facilities in the first semester of 2026

asr-000168
00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:26.300
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The CHR also regularly provides assistance to persons deprived of liberty

asr-000169
00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:31.160
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: 2,503 PDLs were assisted in 2025

asr-000170
00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:39.840
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: while 1,875 PDLs have been assisted for the first semester of 2026

asr-000171
00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:46.920
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The Commission's current financial and human resources for its POD visitation program

asr-000172
00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:56.280
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: allows it to visit, on average, only one-third of the recorded 2,920 detention facilities

asr-000173
00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:59.320
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and, at most, one visit annually

asr-000174
00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:08.300
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: This is precisely why the Commission welcomes the DBM's grant of P16,019,000

asr-000175
00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:12.140
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: to expand the POD visitation program of the Commission

asr-000176
00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:17.420
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: This will allow us to reach more facilities, identify risks earlier,

asr-000177
00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:22.360
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: recommend corrective measures, and help prevent human rights violations before they occur

asr-000178
00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:27.090
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The Commission works

asr-000179
00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.850
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The Commission's work

asr-000180
00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:37.150
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: is not limited to investigating human rights violations after they happen

asr-000181
00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:42.070
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The CHR has the constitutional mandate to establish a continuing program

asr-000182
00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:49.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: of research, education, and information to enhance respect for the primacy of human rights

asr-000183
00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:56.730
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Through its Human Rights Institute and the Lakbay Karapatan Tungo sa Kamalayan or LAKARAN program

asr-000184
00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:58.730
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and other information campaigns,

asr-000185
00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:10.690
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: the CHR has implemented 1,761 and served 122,950 clients in 2025

asr-000186
00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:17.530
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: For the first semester of 2026, the CHR has conducted 823 activities,

asr-000187
00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:23.930
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: reaching 51,716 clients for this year

asr-000188
00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:28.850
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Under the policy advisory services.

asr-000189
00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:29.870
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So,

asr-000190
00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:36.630
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: under the Constitution, the CHR is also tasked with monitoring Philippine government's compliance

asr-000191
00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:39.650
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: with international treaty obligations on human rights

asr-000192
00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:43.830
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and providing the government with policy guidance on human rights

asr-000193
00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:52.210
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The CHR fulfills this mandate by issuing position papers, policy advisories, and situation reports

asr-000194
00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:57.870
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: For 2025, the CHR has released 127 issuances,

asr-000196
00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:04.110
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: while 94 have already been issued for the first semester of 2026

asr-000197
00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:10.070
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So we are still on track as to our accomplishment

asr-000198
00:18:10.070 --> 00:18:17.210
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The CHR also regularly conducts community-based dialogues or CBDs with rights holders

asr-000199
00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:20.370
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: to address localized human rights issues

asr-000200
00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:25.590
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: For 2025, a total of 34 CBDs have been conducted,

asr-000201
00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:28.650
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: while 16 CBDs have been organized,

asr-000202
00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:31.670
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: for the first semester of 2026

asr-000203
00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:39.190
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: We also regularly issue press statements to highlight pressing or urgent human rights concerns,

asr-000204
00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:43.550
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: laud government agencies' best practices and human rights,

asr-000205
00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:48.370
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and to celebrate key international and domestic human rights milestones

asr-000206
00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:54.830
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: For 2025, the CHR has issued 142 press statements

asr-000207
00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:57.870
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and 160 Obligasyon at Karapatan, or

asr-000211
00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:01.150
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: OK Yan sa Human Rights social media cards.

asr-000212
00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:12.390
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: To this end, the CHR respectfully forwards its proposed activities for support under Tier 2.

asr-000213
00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:17.990
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Allow me to quickly go over them, ranked by priority.

asr-000214
00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:26.970
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So for the CHR prioritizes the enhancement of its productivity to ensure efficient delivery of services

asr-000215
00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:34.090
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and requests further support in the amount of 108.237 million

asr-000216
00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:43.130
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: for the implementation of its expanded Places of Deprivation of Liberty Visitation Program and Torture Prevention.

asr-000217
00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:49.350
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: This also includes support for augmenting mandatory expenses in the central and regional offices.

asr-000218
00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:55.290
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: This priority is in line with the current administration's trust on digital transformation.

asr-000219
00:19:55.290 --> 00:20:05.040
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: For Priority Numbers 2 and 3, the Human Rights Action Center and Human Rights Cities,

asr-000220
00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:16.640
