asr-000221
00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:25.000
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: for external clients, specifically for Human Rights Action Center officers and local government units

asr-000222
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:27.580
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: towards the development of human rights cities.

asr-000223
00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:32.400
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and strengthening human rights based approaches to governance.

asr-000224
00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:37.080
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: This will support the mainstreaming of human rights principles and services at the barangay level

asr-000225
00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:43.800
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and support the implementation of the joint memorandums circular between the DILG and the Commission on Human Rights.

asr-000226
00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:51.320
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: We also propose investments in our information systems for a total of 10.114 million

asr-000227
00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:57.700
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: for the continued support and maintenance of the CHR's current digital case management sistem

asr-000228
00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:00.040
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and general administration systems.

asr-000229
00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:03.500
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Continuing from the last slides,

asr-000230
00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:06.900
