asr-000462
00:29:56.920 --> 00:29:58.440
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: pagsali sa ICC?

asr-000463
00:30:00.980 --> 00:30:04.640
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Madam Chair, if I may be allowed.

asr-000464
00:30:06.020 --> 00:30:08.780
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Yes, you are recognized, Chairperson Richard.

asr-000465
00:30:09.960 --> 00:30:24.700
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Tama po. Patuloy pa rin naman po ang aming stand and advocacy for the rejoining of our country sa International Criminal Court or the Rome Statute.

asr-000466
00:30:24.700 --> 00:30:36.680
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So, katuwang po nito, ang ginagawa po ng komisyon ay continuous po ang ating pag-issue ng press statement and public pronouncements,

asr-000467
00:30:37.740 --> 00:30:46.000
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: development and dissemination of infographics or IEC materials, media engagement and public information activities,

asr-000468
00:30:46.660 --> 00:30:51.820
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and use of online platforms to consolidate ICC-related information.

asr-000469
00:30:51.820 --> 00:30:54.660
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Hindi po kasi parte ang komisyon.

asr-000470
00:30:54.700 --> 00:31:06.840
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Sa treaty negotiations or informal decisions on ICC, ang role po natin ay monitor, human rights monitor,

asr-000471
00:31:07.080 --> 00:31:20.200
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: meaning we can only send recommendations to the concerned agencies of the government upang makatulong sa advocacy na pag-rejoin sa ICC.

asr-000472
00:31:20.200 --> 00:31:23.740
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Ngunit, katulad po ng nasabi ko,

asr-000473
00:31:24.360 --> 00:31:24.680
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: ang komisyon,

asr-000474
00:31:24.700 --> 00:31:34.420
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: ang komisyon po ay patuloy at consistent po sa kanya stand na ang Pilipinas po ay mas nararapat na sumali ulit sa ICC.

asr-000475
00:31:35.680 --> 00:31:47.680
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Madam Chair, meron po ba tayong formal recommendation, policy paper, advisory that we have addressed to various duty bearers reflecting this position and this recommendation?

asr-000476
00:31:47.680 --> 00:31:54.680
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: At kung meron po, sino-sino mga duty bearers po yung pinagpaabutan natin na

asr-000477
00:31:54.700 --> 00:31:55.960
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: mga policy recommendations na ito?

asr-000478
00:31:58.700 --> 00:32:00.320
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Madam Chair, meron po.

asr-000479
00:32:02.840 --> 00:32:16.920
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Meron po tayo na isyong eight press statements related sa ICC, including the effects of Philippines withdrawal from the ICC,

asr-000480
00:32:18.140 --> 00:32:21.100
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: the government's decision not to rejoin the ICC,

asr-000481
00:32:21.100 --> 00:32:26.760
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: the ICC's pre-trial chamber's authorization to proceed with investigation,

asr-000482
00:32:26.780 --> 00:32:40.280
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: denial of the Philippine government's appeal to suspend the ICC probe and the issuance of warrant of arrest by the ICC in relation to the alleged crime against humanity involving the former president.

asr-000483
00:32:40.280 --> 00:32:56.740
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So, then we also issued an EJK report which has been forwarded to all national government agencies including the DOJ, Philippine National Police, the PDEA, and others.

asr-000486
00:32:57.100 --> 00:33:02.120
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Madam Chair, marami pong salamat sa ating chairperson ng CHR.

asr-000487
00:33:02.120 --> 00:33:06.200
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: This is a related point po to the earlier question.

asr-000488
00:33:06.880 --> 00:33:08.380
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ngayon po, mahalagang turning point.

asr-000489
00:33:08.880 --> 00:33:15.320
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sa human rights discourse sa Pilipinas, ang paglilitis kay former President Rodrigo Duterte.

asr-000490
00:33:15.900 --> 00:33:19.620
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: But narratives online and offline tell you otherwise.

asr-000491
00:33:20.140 --> 00:33:25.880
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Patuloy po ang pambababoy, pambabalahura, at pagdismiss sa mga biktima ng drug war.

asr-000492
00:33:26.780 --> 00:33:31.880
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ano po ba kung meron man ang efforts ng CHR para labanan ang ganito po mga narratives?

asr-000493
00:33:37.780 --> 00:33:46.780
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Regarding extrajudicial killing, EJK in relation to the drug war, patuloy po yung investigation ng komisyon.

asr-000494
00:33:46.900 --> 00:33:52.420
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Nabanggit ko po ng mga nakaraang mga hearings on budget deliberation ng Commission on Human Rights.

asr-000495
00:33:53.080 --> 00:34:01.140
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Yung mga efforts na ginawa ng komisyon sa investigasyon at mga problema na na-encounter.

asr-000496
00:34:01.160 --> 00:34:13.620
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: At sa ngayon, patuloy pa rin po namin binabalikan yung mga kaso upang mabuo at ultimately matapos na po yung ating investigation tungkol dito.

asr-000497
00:34:14.380 --> 00:34:24.480
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Gayun din po, patuloy pa rin naman po yung ating assistance sa mga victims or families of victims.

asr-000498
00:34:26.280 --> 00:34:32.880
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Isa po sa mga accomplishment ng komisyon patungkol po dito,

asr-000499
00:34:33.020 --> 00:34:52.320
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So, eto po, may kinreate po kasing task force ang komisyon na nag-review, nag-re-evaluate, nag-reopen ng mga cases.

asr-000500
00:34:56.440 --> 00:35:00.680
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Totaling to 493 reinvestigated cases.

asr-000501
00:35:06.550 --> 00:35:12.110
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: 140 cases na po yung for disposition nitong task force na ito.

asr-000502
00:35:12.130 --> 00:35:13.490
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Madam Chair, while we appreciate...

asr-000503
00:35:13.670 --> 00:35:17.770
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: We appreciate the efforts of the CHR in the reopening of these cases.

asr-000504
00:35:17.970 --> 00:35:21.530
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Napapansin lang po kasi ng marami, particular po yung nasa community,

asr-000505
00:35:21.750 --> 00:35:30.290
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: that CHR's voice is notably absent from the public discourse surrounding the ICC proceedings of former President Rodrigo Duterte.

asr-000506
00:35:30.730 --> 00:35:33.090
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Siguro po, humble appeal to the CHR.

asr-000507
00:35:33.650 --> 00:35:42.270
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Yung drug war victims po and their families deserve to know that the CHR has always stood and will stand with them in their pursuit of justice.

asr-000508
00:35:42.270 --> 00:35:46.970
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kung naging very vocal po tayo on the issue of rejoining the ICC,

asr-000509
00:35:47.170 --> 00:35:52.030
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: sana ganun rin po tayo, ganun ka-vocal sa pag-suporta doon sa mga biktima po ng EJK

asr-000510
00:35:52.030 --> 00:36:02.650
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: na ngayon po ay patuloy na binababoy sa daang mga masasamang puwersa habang ongoing po ang trial ni former President Rodrigo Duterte.

asr-000511
00:36:02.950 --> 00:36:07.970
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: I cannot overemphasize the role of CHR in reshaping public discourse on human rights.

asr-000512
00:36:07.970 --> 00:36:11.710
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Alam po natin, tayo ay nasa panahon ng recovery sa ngayon.

asr-000513
00:36:11.710 --> 00:36:15.650
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sa mahabang panahon po, na-demonize ang human rights sa Pilipinas.

asr-000514
00:36:16.150 --> 00:36:20.910
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: At may pagkakatoon po tayo ngayong panahon ito para itama yung pagkakamaling iyon.

asr-000515
00:36:21.170 --> 00:36:34.310
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: And we hope that we start that with rectifying these false narratives na ngayon po ay bastalong lumalaganap because of the ongoing ICC trial of former President Duterte.

asr-000516
00:36:35.330 --> 00:36:40.050
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Let me move to the last theme of my questions for this afternoon.

asr-000517
00:36:40.050 --> 00:36:47.490
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: The CHR previously announced its intention to strengthen work on the relationship between corruption and human rights.

asr-000518
00:36:48.370 --> 00:36:56.390
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Nag-adapt na po ba tayo ng policies, investigative framework, or strategic plans para i-frame ang corruption bilang isang human rights concern?

asr-000519
00:36:57.550 --> 00:37:04.010
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Yes, Madam Chair. Mayroon na pong ginawang activities and policies on ang Commission.

asr-000520
00:37:04.010 --> 00:37:10.010
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: In fact, we conducted two public symposiums on corruption.

asr-000521
00:37:10.050 --> 00:37:20.030
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: One on corruption and human rights upang alamin yung interrelation ng corruption and its effect on human rights.

asr-000522
00:37:20.670 --> 00:37:39.570
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Ito po ay ginawa ng Commission at in attendance po dito ay some government agencies and civil society organizations as well as, of course, Your Honor, umattend po kayo doon under the focal chief of Commissioner Beda A. Epres.

asr-000523
00:37:40.050 --> 00:37:47.210
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: And one activity is conducted by Commissioner Maria Amifaith S. Fider-Reyes.

asr-000524
00:37:48.370 --> 00:37:53.390
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Madam Chair, thank you very much again for the efforts of the Commission in this area.

asr-000525
00:37:53.390 --> 00:38:08.030
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: At siguro po, mahalagang tanungin, para po may pagpatuloy yung trabaho natin dito sa pagbalangkas sa usapin ng korupsyon bilang isang human rights violation at human rights concern, ano po ba yung kailangan resources ng CHR para dito?

asr-000526
00:38:10.690 --> 00:38:11.150
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Yun pong...

asr-000527
00:38:11.810 --> 00:38:23.170
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Siguro po, Madam Chair, ibabalik ko lamang po doon sa aming tier 2 request or proposals pagkat ito po ay makakatulong sa pagtupad ng Commission sa kanyang mandato.

asr-000528
00:38:23.930 --> 00:38:25.590
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Thank you very much, Madam Chair.

asr-000529
00:38:25.750 --> 00:38:30.810
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: The government and the public must recognize that corruption is a human rights concern.

asr-000530
00:38:31.330 --> 00:38:37.190
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sa bawat piso na pupunta sa bulsa ng iilan, maraming karapatang pantao ang nilalapastangan.

asr-000531
00:38:37.490 --> 00:38:40.970
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: At ito pong ating investment sa Commission on Human Rights.

asr-000532
00:38:41.810 --> 00:38:54.670
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: is not just about framing human rights as a civil political issue, but more than that, a socio-economic concern given the massive corruption happening in our country.

asr-000533
00:38:54.670 --> 00:39:07.450
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: That's why Akbayan Partylist is fully supportive of restoring the tier 2 proposal of the Commission para po tunay na masabi natin sa Pilipinas, pinahahalagahan natin ang karapatang pantao.

asr-000534
00:39:07.710 --> 00:39:09.010
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Maraming salamat, Madam Chair.

asr-000535
00:39:10.190 --> 00:39:11.670
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Thank you, Representative.

asr-000536
00:39:11.810 --> 00:39:13.170
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Thank you, Representative Perci Cendaña.

asr-000537
00:39:13.870 --> 00:39:18.170
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Of course, before we proceed, I would like to recognize na dagdagan na po tayo.

asr-000538
00:39:18.810 --> 00:39:30.030
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: So, nandito pong ating Vice Chair, our former Dean, napakagaling po nating attorney, Vice Chair Rufus Rodriguez of Cagayan de Oro.

asr-000539
00:39:30.850 --> 00:39:31.950
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Good afternoon po, sir.

asr-000540
00:39:31.950 --> 00:39:41.490
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: And also our Vice Chair, Assistant Majority Leader, Representative Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong of Lanao del Sur.

asr-000541
00:39:41.810 --> 00:39:52.190
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: And also our Senior Deputy Minority Leader, Leila M. de Lima of ML Party-list.

asr-000542
00:39:52.270 --> 00:39:53.670
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Good afternoon po, ma'am and sir.

asr-000543
00:39:54.290 --> 00:39:54.830
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Good afternoon.

asr-000544
00:39:56.370 --> 00:40:05.210
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Our next Interpolator, Vice Chair Rufus Rodriguez.

asr-000545
00:40:05.210 --> 00:40:08.470
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-000546
00:40:09.090 --> 00:40:11.210
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Chairperson Maria Cristina.

asr-000547
00:40:11.810 --> 00:40:13.290
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Chairperson Maria Cristina Talavera-Lopez.

asr-000548
00:40:13.730 --> 00:40:16.710
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you very much for giving the opportunity.

asr-000549
00:40:16.930 --> 00:40:28.410
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: My distinguished colleagues, a pleasant good afternoon to our family of the Commission on Human Rights, Richard, the chairman, Richard Palpal-latoc.

asr-000550
00:40:28.410 --> 00:40:40.410
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And I would also like to welcome Judge Maria Amifaith S. Fider-Reyes, who taught in San Jose Recoletos, my fellow, my...

asr-000551
00:40:41.810 --> 00:40:47.270
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: colleague, my, my same Recoletos School of San Sebastian where I was Dean.

asr-000552
00:40:48.050 --> 00:40:51.070
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Justice Monina Zenarosa, thank you for making me win.

asr-000553
00:40:51.610 --> 00:40:54.010
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I had at least three cases with you and I won all of them.

asr-000554
00:40:55.270 --> 00:40:55.850
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-000555
00:40:55.930 --> 00:40:57.310
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Magaling yan si ma'am.

asr-000556
00:40:57.930 --> 00:40:59.450
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Tsaka stricta yan sa korte.

asr-000557
00:41:00.250 --> 00:41:02.070
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, thank you, ma'am, for being here.

asr-000558
00:41:02.370 --> 00:41:05.950
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you for my victories, legal victories in your court.

asr-000559
00:41:06.690 --> 00:41:11.530
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And we have Faydah Dumarpa, the daughter of my good friends, the Commissioner,

asr-000560
00:41:11.810 --> 00:41:24.250
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: the Congresswoman, Dumarpa, and our Executive Director, the Commissioner, Lawrence Salazar, and all the rest.

asr-000561
00:41:24.250 --> 00:41:32.350
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I am here, Mr. Chairman, to really support the budget of the CHR, including its increase,

asr-000562
00:41:33.210 --> 00:41:39.730
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: because I have seen the reduction of the budget of the CHR from last year's level.

asr-000563
00:41:40.590 --> 00:41:41.750
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: In fact, Mr. Chairman, I...

asr-000564
00:41:41.810 --> 00:41:46.330
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I am a co-author of the bill strengthening the CHR.

asr-000565
00:41:46.990 --> 00:41:54.710
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And we hope that this will be passed because I have here my fellow co-authors who are very interested to strengthen the CHR.

asr-000566
00:41:55.250 --> 00:41:56.450
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, we are here for that.

asr-000567
00:41:56.450 --> 00:42:04.770
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Now, going to the budget, so, as a premise, I support the strengthening of the Commission on Human Rights.

asr-000568
00:42:05.250 --> 00:42:11.450
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: But this budget will not strengthen them because we have reduced from 1.3...

asr-000569
00:42:11.810 --> 00:42:27.410
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: million pesos, 1.3 billion. It has now become 1.2 billion, a decrease of 74 million 882 thousand pesos.

asr-000570
00:42:27.590 --> 00:42:29.230
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Does this include the tier 2?

asr-000571
00:42:30.870 --> 00:42:31.690
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Combined neto?

asr-000572
00:42:32.430 --> 00:42:37.150
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, therefore, you wish that the 74 be restored?

asr-000573
00:42:38.050 --> 00:42:39.630
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And how much is the tier 2?

asr-000574
00:42:39.910 --> 00:42:41.330
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, that we can have everything here.

asr-000575
00:42:41.810 --> 00:42:45.430
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, for tier 1, 74 was removed?

asr-000576
00:42:45.670 --> 00:42:45.970
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Yes.

asr-000577
00:42:46.130 --> 00:42:47.610
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much is your tier 2?

asr-000578
00:42:47.990 --> 00:42:50.050
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: 1.5 billion.

asr-000579
00:42:50.050 --> 00:42:50.850
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: 7.6 billion.

asr-000580
00:42:50.850 --> 00:42:51.170
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Okay.

asr-000581
00:42:51.890 --> 00:42:55.690
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Now, we have given the agencies up to Wednesday next week.

asr-000582
00:42:57.270 --> 00:42:58.230
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I belong to the...

asr-000583
00:42:58.230 --> 00:43:01.310
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I am the vice chair of the Corporations Committee.

asr-000584
00:43:02.170 --> 00:43:09.310
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And can we request you to submit first this tier 1, 74 million,

asr-000585
00:43:09.810 --> 00:43:10.850
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and your...

asr-000586
00:43:11.810 --> 00:43:14.570
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Majority on the 1.4.

asr-000587
00:43:14.650 --> 00:43:17.570
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We don't think that everything will be given,

asr-000588
00:43:18.190 --> 00:43:19.790
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: but you give us the first three,

asr-000589
00:43:20.130 --> 00:43:24.310
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: probably amounting to about 300 to 400 million.

asr-000590
00:43:24.430 --> 00:43:26.050
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: You have to give us the fiscal space.

asr-000591
00:43:26.490 --> 00:43:29.870
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, you submit that to our committee chairman Lopez,

asr-000592
00:43:30.490 --> 00:43:34.130
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: so that our chairman Lopez here will be able to bring that

asr-000593
00:43:34.130 --> 00:43:38.050
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: in our meeting of the vice chairman after Wednesday next week.

asr-000594
00:43:38.050 --> 00:43:41.330
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Will that be okay with you, Chairman Richard?

asr-000595
00:43:41.810 --> 00:43:45.110
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Yes, Honorable Vice Chair.

asr-000596
00:43:45.690 --> 00:43:48.850
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: We appreciate the support of your honor.

asr-000597
00:43:49.570 --> 00:43:52.950
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, as far as the tier 1, what is given to you,

asr-000598
00:43:53.370 --> 00:43:56.150
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: you have a reduction of 34 million.

asr-000599
00:43:56.290 --> 00:43:58.130
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: It's very, very important that it be restored.

asr-000600
00:43:58.770 --> 00:44:01.050
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: For capital outlay also, zero.

asr-000601
00:44:01.730 --> 00:44:02.990
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What are these for?

asr-000602
00:44:03.070 --> 00:44:04.770
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: For the building or for the transportation?

asr-000603
00:44:07.010 --> 00:44:09.810
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Mostly retrofitting.

asr-000604
00:44:09.810 --> 00:44:11.170
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: I see the building.

asr-000605
00:44:11.170 --> 00:44:13.270
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: I see the vehicles.

asr-000606
00:44:14.650 --> 00:44:16.510
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: That is really required.

asr-000607
00:44:16.650 --> 00:44:21.230
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, I hope that this one will be 150 to be restored,

asr-000608
00:44:21.890 --> 00:44:27.930
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: plus 300 to 400 million of your priority in tier 2.

asr-000609
00:44:28.470 --> 00:44:30.110
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We'll try to have increases here.

asr-000610
00:44:30.510 --> 00:44:33.910
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Because anyway, it is Congress, the power of the purse,

asr-000611
00:44:34.070 --> 00:44:35.690
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and with the vice chairman present here,

asr-000612
00:44:36.210 --> 00:44:36.930
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: we'll be able to...

asr-000613
00:44:36.930 --> 00:44:39.770
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Can you give us now the first three priorities of tier 2?

asr-000614
00:44:56.960 --> 00:44:57.520
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So,

asr-000615
00:44:57.520 --> 00:44:59.990
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The top three priorities.

asr-000616
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:05.680
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The priorities would be, of course, strengthening the preventive mandate of the Commission.

asr-000617
00:45:06.020 --> 00:45:15.640
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Meron na pong initial increase na binigay ang DBM dito, but we still request na i-grant po yung remaining.

asr-000618
00:45:16.640 --> 00:45:19.340
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And then, how much is that? How much?

asr-000619
00:45:19.560 --> 00:45:22.580
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Ang naiwan po ay around 4 million na lamang.

asr-000620
00:45:22.580 --> 00:45:27.540
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Ang request po namin ay 21, nabigyan po kami ng additional 16.

asr-000621
00:45:27.540 --> 00:45:33.420
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So, mga 5, which we think, the DBM, then. So, mga 5 po yung remaining.

asr-000622
00:45:33.760 --> 00:45:35.020
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Okay. 5 million. Next.

asr-000623
00:45:35.340 --> 00:45:41.860
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: For number 2 would be the augmentation of mandatory expenses for the central office and regional offices,

asr-000624
00:45:43.200 --> 00:45:47.220
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: amounting to 59,505,000.

asr-000625
00:45:47.380 --> 00:45:51.000
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Okay. Third?

asr-000626
00:45:51.000 --> 00:45:58.580
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: At toko yung, both of them would be, would enhance productivity of the Commission on Human Rights.

asr-000627
00:45:59.360 --> 00:46:05.580
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Amounting to 108,237,000.

asr-000628
00:46:05.580 --> 00:46:14.920
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: And then, next in the priority would be the capacity building program for Human Rights Action Center officers

asr-000629
00:46:14.920 --> 00:46:19.200
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and capacity building of LGUs toward human rights cities.

asr-000630
00:46:19.500 --> 00:46:24.280
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Ito po ay initiative ng Commission to localize human rights work.

asr-000631
00:46:24.500 --> 00:46:25.400
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much will that be?

asr-000632
00:46:25.740 --> 00:46:28.580
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: 18,416,000.

asr-000633
00:46:28.580 --> 00:46:28.980
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Okay.

asr-000634
00:46:29.360 --> 00:46:38.280
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: As well as rollout training for central and regional offices for newly developed CHR information systems.

asr-000635
00:46:38.440 --> 00:46:41.000
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Wala po kami pondo na para po dito.

asr-000636
00:46:41.740 --> 00:46:43.240
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Nasa 10 million po ito.

asr-000637
00:46:44.580 --> 00:46:45.220
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: And then,

asr-000638
00:46:49.500 --> 00:46:59.140
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: ano po, mostly databases and either ISSP activities amounting to 227 million.

asr-000639
00:46:59.360 --> 00:47:06.120
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So, total, for all the, so 10 million lang po yung ano.

asr-000640
00:47:06.240 --> 00:47:12.080
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So, total po ng priority would be 227 million.

asr-000641
00:47:12.480 --> 00:47:17.620
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: And of course, Your Honor, we would like also to request additional budget for,

asr-000642
00:47:18.160 --> 00:47:24.560
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: kasi po meron po kaming role sa global and regional NHRI organizations.

asr-000643
00:47:24.560 --> 00:47:27.880
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: We are status A accredited.

asr-000644
00:47:28.240 --> 00:47:29.340
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: National Human Rights.

asr-000645
00:47:29.360 --> 00:47:40.080
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: I personally sit as the chairperson of the Working Group on Business and Human Rights of the Global Alliance of National Human Rights Institution.

asr-000646
00:47:41.440 --> 00:47:48.180
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Yung pong si Commissioner Beda Epres ay umuupo rin sa Intergovernmental Working Group on the Rights of Children.

asr-000647
00:47:49.180 --> 00:47:56.640
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: And then, sa Asia Pacific Region po, I am a member of the Governing Board of the Asia Pacific Forum of National Human Rights Institution.

asr-000648
00:47:56.640 --> 00:47:58.640
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: As well as the Southeast Asia.

asr-000649
00:47:59.360 --> 00:48:01.700
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: As well as the Southeast Asia National Human Rights Institution Forum.

asr-000650
00:48:02.140 --> 00:48:11.840
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: This would require, of course, budget so that we can fulfill our roles in this regional and global organizations.

asr-000651
00:48:12.940 --> 00:48:20.160
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Sa ngayon po, ang request po namin under Tier 2, only 1.9 million.

asr-000652
00:48:20.840 --> 00:48:21.200
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Your Honor.

asr-000653
