Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: yung incidence of torture.

asr-001344
01:14:49.270 --> 01:14:51.270
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At syempre gusto natin na hindi na ito maulit

asr-001345
01:14:51.270 --> 01:14:55.270
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and through the budget nga na maibibigay ay magawa yan.

asr-001346
01:14:55.270 --> 01:14:56.270
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kaya po ba yun, Mr. Chair?

asr-001347
01:14:56.270 --> 01:14:58.270
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Yes. Yes, Madam Chair.

asr-001348
01:14:58.270 --> 01:14:59.270
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-001349
01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:05.620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Important po na magawa po ng CHR yung mandate niya at syempre in support po tayo sa pagtaas ng budget.

asr-001350
01:15:05.760 --> 01:15:10.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Lalo na po itong number one dahil ito po yung pinag-uusapan natin ngayon, di ba po?

asr-001351
01:15:11.620 --> 01:15:16.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kamusta po ba yung mga bahay pag-asa para maalagaan yung mga kapakanan ng kabataan?

asr-001352
01:15:16.960 --> 01:15:23.860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Paano po ba natin may ensure ng ating mga PDLs ay hindi po unduly deprived of their human rights?

asr-001353
01:15:24.020 --> 01:15:28.440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kailangan po, nagagawa ng CHR yung mandato sa pag-check

asr-001354
01:15:28.440 --> 01:15:36.780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and through the means and measures na mas nagagawa at hindi ito, as you said niya po, uncoordinated.

asr-001355
01:15:36.780 --> 01:15:47.780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My next question is in relation to the 2025 National Inquiry of the CHR on red-tagging.

asr-001356
01:15:48.840 --> 01:15:56.740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So this representation welcomes the executive summary na nirelease po ng CHR

asr-001357
01:15:56.740 --> 01:15:57.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na

asr-001358
01:15:57.460 --> 01:16:05.320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: report niya po that it remains an entrenched systemic practice that acts as a precursor to physical harassment,

asr-001359
01:16:05.840 --> 01:16:08.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: arbitrary detention, and extrajudicial killings.

asr-001360
01:16:08.500 --> 01:16:14.980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And meron pong preliminary recommendations ang CHR included po doon yung criminalizing yung red-tagging

asr-001361
01:16:14.980 --> 01:16:17.560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: which this representation has filed a bill for.

asr-001362
01:16:18.180 --> 01:16:24.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So we eagerly await the full report but habang hinihintay po natin yun,

asr-001363
01:16:24.720 --> 01:16:27.440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: gusto po natin itanong sa commission.

asr-001364
01:16:27.460 --> 01:16:36.540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Given that the findings say that red-tagging acts as an immediate precursor to arbitrary detention and extrajudicial killings,

asr-001365
01:16:37.060 --> 01:16:40.300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: how much po sa MOOE ninyo, kung meron man,

asr-001366
01:16:40.660 --> 01:16:46.280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ang directly allocated to operationalized rapid response legal deployment teams,

asr-001367
01:16:46.780 --> 01:16:51.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: especially for rural and conflict-afflicted areas where access to counsel is severely limited?

asr-001368
01:16:53.940 --> 01:16:57.140
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Hingi lang po ako ng permiso, Madam Chair, to check our...

asr-001369
01:16:58.800 --> 01:17:06.280
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Wala po kasi kaming budget dedicated for red-tagging.

asr-001370
01:17:06.280 --> 01:17:08.440
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: For it right now. Dahil bago rin po yung...

asr-001371
01:17:08.440 --> 01:17:12.060
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Opo. Naka-lump po siya sa aming protection service.

asr-001372
01:17:13.640 --> 01:17:26.980
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Ang total po kasi ng aming budget, allotment for protection program ay 323,278,000.

asr-001373
01:17:28.380 --> 01:17:29.440
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Ito po yung...

asr-001374
01:17:30.340 --> 01:17:34.100
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: kabuuan ng Human Rights Protection Service.

asr-001375
01:17:34.500 --> 01:17:37.460
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So kung yung kabuuan, ibig po sabihin nito ay investigation,

asr-001376
01:17:38.920 --> 01:17:42.420
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: legal services, legal assistance,

asr-001377
01:17:42.940 --> 01:17:46.200
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: forensic services,

asr-001378
01:17:47.520 --> 01:17:49.280
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: witness assistance and protection,

asr-001379
01:17:51.690 --> 01:17:52.270
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and then,

asr-001380
01:17:53.310 --> 01:17:58.870
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: humahati pa po dyan yung budget for the prevention service, yung pong jail visitation.

asr-001381
01:17:59.750 --> 01:18:01.290
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So, hindi po ako makapagbibigyan.

asr-001382
01:18:01.650 --> 01:18:10.150
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Hindi po ako makapagbibigyan ng exact figure dedicated for this activity na tinatanong po ninyo, Your Honor.

asr-001383
01:18:10.910 --> 01:18:17.910
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: But, to give you the figure in totality, yun po siya.

asr-001384
01:18:18.270 --> 01:18:23.370
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Protection service. Kabuuan po ito ng protection program ng komisyon.

asr-001385
01:18:24.870 --> 01:18:29.690
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And siguro, tanong ko na lang din po, given na may report po tayo,

asr-001386
01:18:29.690 --> 01:18:31.630
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and then may recommendations tayo,

asr-001387
01:18:31.650 --> 01:18:36.070
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: bahagi po ba yung recommendations, yung pagbuuan ng protocols or guidelines,

asr-001388
01:18:36.070 --> 01:18:40.810
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kung paano po gamitin yung pondo na ito para po mag-rapid response kung kailangan po?

asr-001389
01:18:40.810 --> 01:18:45.610
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Yes po. Kasama po yun sa recommendation and of course, the strategy of the commission.

asr-001390
01:18:45.610 --> 01:18:50.210
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Maaari po bang makahingi din po ng kopya ang representation na ito through the committee

asr-001391
01:18:50.210 --> 01:18:52.410
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kung nabuo na po yung guidelines?

asr-001392
01:18:52.410 --> 01:18:56.590
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Yes. Opo. I-submit po namin yung ito.

asr-001393
01:18:56.590 --> 01:19:00.990
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you very much. And siguro, ang final manifestation ko na lang din po,

asr-001394
01:19:01.650 --> 01:19:09.450
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: dahil red tagging also increasingly operates through digital platforms, doxing, deepfix, and coordinated online campaigns,

asr-001395
01:19:09.450 --> 01:19:17.950
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: may funding po din sanang allocated and guidelines provided towards digital forensic tools, cyber threat monitoring systems,

asr-001396
01:19:17.950 --> 01:19:22.350
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and secure database infrastructure to preserve digital evidence.

asr-001397
01:19:22.350 --> 01:19:26.710
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Lalo na po mas nakikita natin yung state-backed vilification.

asr-001398
01:19:26.710 --> 01:19:31.490
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And of course, similarly sa pagtingin at pag-alam natin,

asr-001399
01:19:31.490 --> 01:19:38.390
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na may mga areas na mas frequent yung human rights violations or even yung incidents of torture.

asr-001400
01:19:38.390 --> 01:19:41.490
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I'm sure that is also the case for red tagging.

asr-001401
01:19:41.490 --> 01:19:52.150
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: For example, may mas high-risk regions like Southern Tagalog, Bicol, Negros, Northern Mindanao, na statistically higher sila.

asr-001402
01:19:52.150 --> 01:20:01.290
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So maaari po sana ma-consider yung internal allocation formula na, syempre, gusto natin spread out yung mga,

asr-001403
01:20:01.290 --> 01:20:07.990
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: puwersa, recurso natin. Pero ang reality ay may mga iilang regions na mas kailangan ng focus.

asr-001404
01:20:07.990 --> 01:20:14.590
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang dulo naman po nito, Madam Chair, nakikita natin na ang human rights situation sa Pilipinas,

asr-001405
01:20:14.590 --> 01:20:17.990
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: hindi po natin nakikita yung improvement.

asr-001406
01:20:17.990 --> 01:20:29.790
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And so, yung mas dagdag na pondo, suporta sa CHR, at lalo na rin po yung sa pag-capacitate at pag-empower ng mga civil society organizations,

asr-001407
01:20:29.790 --> 01:20:31.290
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: people's organizations,

asr-001408
01:20:31.290 --> 01:20:38.790
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na mapag-aralan nila kung ano yung human rights nila, mapanghawakan, maprotektahan nila nang sama-sama yung instrument and key

asr-001409
01:20:38.790 --> 01:20:44.790
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: para po malabanan yung systematic violations na nararanasan natin ngayon.

asr-001410
01:20:44.790 --> 01:20:51.790
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: That's all, Madam Chair. Maraming salamat po. And of course, tuloy-tuloy po sana ang gawain ng CHR.

asr-001411
01:20:51.790 --> 01:20:56.790
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Thank you, Representative Ko, for your manifestation of support, of course.

asr-001412
01:20:56.790 --> 01:20:59.790
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Before we proceed, I would like to recognize

asr-001413
01:20:59.790 --> 01:21:05.790
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: our former President, Representative Gloria Macapagal-Arroyo of Pampanga.

asr-001414
01:21:05.790 --> 01:21:10.790
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: And also, Representative J. Vergara of Nueva Ecija.

asr-001415
01:21:10.790 --> 01:21:17.790
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Nandito rin po kasama natin si Representative Sara Ilago of Gabriela Partilis.

asr-001416
01:21:17.790 --> 01:21:27.490
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Moving forward po, from majority, I would like to recognize Representative J. Vergara.

asr-001417
01:21:27.490 --> 01:21:29.490
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-001418
01:21:29.490 --> 01:21:31.490
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Simple lamang po.

asr-001419
01:21:31.490 --> 01:21:35.490
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Magandang hapon po sa inyo, CHR family.

asr-001420
01:21:35.490 --> 01:21:42.490
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: In deference to my uncle, who was a chairperson.

asr-001421
01:21:42.490 --> 01:21:48.490
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ang pangalan po niya ay Atty. Sedfrey Ordoñez.

asr-001422
01:21:48.490 --> 01:21:52.490
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: At naging chairperson po ng CHR,

asr-001423
01:21:52.490 --> 01:21:57.490
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: nagmamanifest lang po ako ng buong pusong suporta sa inyo. Maraming salamat po.

asr-001424
01:21:57.490 --> 01:21:59.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Maraming salamat po, Kong.

asr-001425
01:21:59.490 --> 01:22:06.490
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Thank you. Talagang yan lang po ang ipinunta po dito ni Representative Vergara para sa manifestation of support.

asr-001426
01:22:06.490 --> 01:22:14.490
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Next, from minority, Senior Deputy Minority Leader, Laila de Lima. You are recognized.

asr-001427
01:22:14.490 --> 01:22:21.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Maraming salamat po, Madam Chair. Good afternoon to everyone. Good afternoon to my colleagues. Good afternoon to the CHR family.

asr-001428
01:22:21.490 --> 01:22:27.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Alam niyo, I was looking at the faces and mukhang dalawa o tatlo na lang yung mga familiar faces sa akin.

asr-001429
01:22:27.490 --> 01:22:29.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: O lima pala.

asr-001430
01:22:29.490 --> 01:22:35.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Lima pala because most of them, I think, have retired already and they are really new faces.

asr-001431
01:22:35.490 --> 01:22:41.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Including, of course, the chairperson and the commissioners of the commission.

asr-001432
01:22:41.490 --> 01:22:45.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Well, some of my questions have been touched already.

asr-001433
01:22:45.490 --> 01:22:53.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Although, I came here also to express my full, to manifest my full support for the budget of the CHR

asr-001434
01:22:53.490 --> 01:22:56.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: and to appeal for the restoration of

asr-001435
01:22:56.490 --> 01:22:59.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: of whatever it needed to be restored.

asr-001436
01:22:59.490 --> 01:23:03.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: You're the Tier 2. You're Tier 2 proposals.

asr-001437
01:23:03.490 --> 01:23:10.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Para sa akin kasi, this committee must look at the CHR budget

asr-001438
01:23:10.490 --> 01:23:13.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: not simply as another item in the NEP,

asr-001439
01:23:13.490 --> 01:23:19.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: but as an investment in the constitutional guarantees that protect every Filipino.

asr-001440
01:23:19.490 --> 01:23:25.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: And in a democracy, Madam Chair, there can be no more important investment

asr-001441
01:23:25.490 --> 01:23:31.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: than the protection, promotion, and prevention of human rights.

asr-001442
01:23:31.490 --> 01:23:35.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Ang unang tanong ko po, we all know the three core mandates of the CHR.

asr-001443
01:23:35.490 --> 01:23:37.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: These are the three P's.

asr-001444
01:23:37.490 --> 01:23:40.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Prevention, protection, and promotion.

asr-001445
01:23:40.490 --> 01:23:48.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Which of these three core mandates that CHR has been experiencing a lot of challenges?

asr-001446
01:23:48.490 --> 01:23:54.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: In terms of resources and in terms also of implementation of your core programs

asr-001447
01:23:54.490 --> 01:23:56.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: and activities.

asr-001448
01:23:56.490 --> 01:24:02.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: And if you're experiencing those challenges, can you tell us why exactly?

asr-001449
01:24:02.490 --> 01:24:05.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Madam Chair, thank you for the question.

asr-001450
01:24:05.490 --> 01:24:14.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: In terms of resources, the most challenging mandate of the Commission would be the prevention service.

asr-001451
01:24:14.490 --> 01:24:22.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: As I mentioned earlier, the prevention service is sharing budget with the protection service.

asr-001452
01:24:22.490 --> 01:24:29.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: There was no dedicated allocation for the prevention service

asr-001453
01:24:29.490 --> 01:24:33.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: except for a small chunk from the protection service.

asr-001454
01:24:33.490 --> 01:24:42.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So that's why I was saying earlier that our field investigators would include jail visits

asr-001455
01:24:42.490 --> 01:24:48.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: when they proceed to conducting investigation in the field.

asr-001456
01:24:48.490 --> 01:24:50.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: So aside from the investigation,

asr-001457
01:24:50.490 --> 01:24:52.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: they conduct those visitations?

asr-001458
01:24:52.490 --> 01:24:53.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Yes, ma'am.

asr-001459
01:24:53.490 --> 01:24:54.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Para makatipid?

asr-001460
01:24:54.490 --> 01:24:56.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Para makatipid.

asr-001461
01:24:56.490 --> 01:24:58.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: What else?

asr-001462
01:24:58.490 --> 01:25:04.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: In the prevention itself, your cases, are there backlogs?

asr-001463
01:25:04.490 --> 01:25:05.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Cases?

asr-001464
01:25:05.490 --> 01:25:06.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Yes.

asr-001465
01:25:06.490 --> 01:25:13.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: We have actually resolved the majority of the case backlogs of the Commission.

asr-001466
01:25:13.490 --> 01:25:19.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So from 28,000 cases,

asr-001467
01:25:19.490 --> 01:25:24.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: from 1987 to 2025,

asr-001468
01:25:24.490 --> 01:25:30.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: we have resolved 95.8% of the backlog cases.

asr-001469
01:25:30.490 --> 01:25:38.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: And that would translate to around 27,000 cases concluded by the CHR.

asr-001470
01:25:38.490 --> 01:25:48.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So we have a pending case of around 1,200 backlog cases.

asr-001471
01:25:48.490 --> 01:25:49.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Okay.

asr-001472
01:25:49.490 --> 01:25:51.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: What about the drug war killings?

asr-001473
01:25:51.490 --> 01:25:54.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: What is the status of the investigation of the CHR?

asr-001474
01:25:54.490 --> 01:26:02.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: I have not been aware of any updates on the status of investigation into drug war killings

asr-001475
01:26:02.490 --> 01:26:04.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: because I suppose in spite of the ICC,

asr-001476
01:26:04.490 --> 01:26:09.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: CHR continues to do its own investigation of these drug war killings.

asr-001477
01:26:09.490 --> 01:26:13.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: And in conjunction especially with the DOJ,

asr-001478
01:26:13.490 --> 01:26:15.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: yung AO35 na minensyon nyo kanina,

asr-001479
01:26:15.490 --> 01:26:18.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: it's good to know that you are still supporting

asr-001480
01:26:18.490 --> 01:26:19.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: that.

asr-001481
01:26:19.490 --> 01:26:24.490
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: And what exactly is the role of the CHR in the AO35 mechanism?

asr-001482
01:26:24.490 --> 01:26:27.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So, thank you Madam Chair, Your Honor.

asr-001483
01:26:27.490 --> 01:26:31.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: In terms of the drug war cases,

asr-001484
01:26:31.490 --> 01:26:36.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: majority of the cases when we assumed office have already been concluded.

asr-001485
01:26:36.490 --> 01:26:39.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So when we assumed office,

asr-001486
01:26:39.490 --> 01:26:43.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: we decided to reinvestigate some of the cases

asr-001487
01:26:43.490 --> 01:26:47.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: because of the challenges experienced by our investigators.

asr-001488
01:26:47.490 --> 01:26:49.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: During that time.

asr-001489
01:26:49.490 --> 01:26:52.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So as of today,

asr-001490
01:26:52.490 --> 01:27:00.490
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: there are already 493 cases for reinvestigation.

asr-001491
01:27:00.490 --> 01:27:15.500
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: And our task force has concluded 289 cases related to the drug war.

asr-001492
01:27:15.500 --> 01:27:17.500
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: You mentioned reinvestigation?

asr-001493
01:27:17.500 --> 01:27:18.500
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Reinvestigated.

asr-001494
01:27:18.500 --> 01:27:19.500
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Because as I mentioned,

asr-001495
01:27:19.500 --> 01:27:23.500
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: there were challenges encountered by the Commission

asr-001496
01:27:23.500 --> 01:27:26.500
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: during that time in terms of...

asr-001497
01:27:26.500 --> 01:27:30.500
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Those resolved cases have been forwarded already to the DOJ.

asr-001498
01:27:30.500 --> 01:27:32.500
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Most of them were dismissed actually

asr-001499
01:27:32.500 --> 01:27:35.500
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: because of lack of evidence.

asr-001500
01:27:35.500 --> 01:27:38.500
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The challenges as I mentioned are

asr-001501
01:27:38.500 --> 01:27:43.500
