02:25:59.690 --> 02:26:00.930
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-002624
02:26:00.930 --> 02:26:02.570
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So, as men, as...

asr-002625
02:26:02.590 --> 02:26:09.930
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Already answered before when Congressman Laila de Lima asked.

asr-002626
02:26:10.550 --> 02:26:15.130
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: We don't have, the CHR does not have oversight function over the NTF-ELCAC.

asr-002627
02:26:16.130 --> 02:26:26.550
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So we don't have administrative or programmatic oversight of the NTF-ELCAC or the support to the Barangay Development Program.

asr-002628
02:26:26.550 --> 02:26:39.610
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The NTF-ELCAC is an executive mechanism and the implementation and financial administration of the support to the Barangay Development Program are functions of the executive branch.

asr-002629
02:26:41.750 --> 02:26:51.650
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: What we can do is, as I said, monitor the compliance of the government to human rights obligations

asr-002630
02:26:51.650 --> 02:26:57.610
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: and ensure that in the performance of the NTF-ELCAC,

asr-002631
02:26:57.830 --> 02:27:03.070
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: of its mandate, there's no human rights violation committed.

asr-002632
02:27:04.150 --> 02:27:05.630
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: And then what additional demands?

asr-002633
02:27:06.630 --> 02:27:17.350
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: The principal additional demand of the CHR is not the monitoring of the SBDP as a program,

asr-002634
02:27:17.490 --> 02:27:22.810
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: but the increased possibility of human rights concern arising in geographically isolated,

asr-002635
02:27:22.810 --> 02:27:26.630
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: conflict-affected, and otherwise vulnerable communities.

asr-002636
02:27:27.110 --> 02:27:27.810
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Where access to

asr-002637
02:27:27.830 --> 02:27:31.930
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Government institutions and remedies may already be difficult.

asr-002638
02:27:32.690 --> 02:27:40.570
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: So in practical terms, this may require CHR's regional offices to undertake more field-based monitoring,

asr-002639
02:27:40.870 --> 02:27:44.850
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: receive and assess complaints, conduct fact-finding and field investigations,

asr-002640
02:27:46.330 --> 02:27:49.650
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: provide or facilitate appropriate legal and protective assistance,

asr-002641
02:27:50.030 --> 02:27:55.070
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: document alleged violation, and conduct human rights education and community engagement.

asr-002642
02:27:55.510 --> 02:27:59.090
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: Based on the CHR's monitoring,

asr-002643
02:27:59.370 --> 02:28:01.350
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: complaints and public inquiries,

asr-002644
02:28:01.530 --> 02:28:04.350
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: the recurring risks that Congress should consider may include

asr-002645
02:28:04.350 --> 02:28:08.750
CHR Chairperson Richard P. Palpal-latoc: widespread and systemic vilification of human rights defenders

asr-002646
